\tag{fdip}
\title{Reference pairings, adjoints and support projections}
\date{2026-10-20}

\p{A reference pairing represents the adjoint of a field operator.
The [finite field module](fdip-0010) has a perfect counting pairing
over any commutative unital ring. Its represented adjoint is an
ordinary linear product-reversing involution; neither positivity nor
division by two is required.}

\p{A partition of the carrier also splits the field module by
restriction and extension by zero. These reference maps precede the
[paired differences](fdip-0016) and the
[elimination of a chosen summand](fdip-0020).}

